[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112680,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Exophytic sinonasal papilloma is a benign sinonasal tract epithelial neoplasm composed of broad papillary fronds with delicate fibrovascular cores covered by a maturing multilayered epithelium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112681,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "<p>8121/0 Sinonasal papilloma, exophytic</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-30T17:17:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112682,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F00.Y &amp; XH0TP8 Other specified benign neoplasm of middle ear or respiratory system &amp; Sinonasal papilloma, exophytic</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112683,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Schneiderian papilloma, exophytic type; fungiform papilloma; everted papilloma; transitional cell papilloma; septal papilloma; Ringertz tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112684,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112685,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Exophytic sinonasal papillomas usually arise on the lower anterior nasal septum {7837917; 29341451}. As they enlarge, they may secondarily involve the lateral nasal wall, but they rarely originate there. Involvement of the paranasal sinuses is extremely rare. Bilateral lesions are exceptional {7837917; 29341451}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112686,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Typical presenting symptoms include epistaxis and unilateral nasal obstruction caused by a mass lesion. Endoscopy aids in defining the site and extent of disease, but imaging is unnecessary.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112687,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are 2&ndash;10&nbsp;times as common in male patients as female patients, and they typically occur in individuals aged 20&ndash;50&nbsp;years (range: 2&ndash;87&nbsp;years) {3957337; 23883810}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112688,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority of these tumours harbour low-risk HPV (mostly types&nbsp;6 and&nbsp;11) {7837916; 23161522}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112689,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112690,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours present as papillary or warty, grey, pink, or tan growths attached to the nasal septum by a relatively broad base. They range in size up to about 20&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112691,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Exophytic sinonasal papillomas are composed of papillary fronds with fibrovascular cores covered by a proliferative, multilayered epithelium that is 5&ndash;20&nbsp;cells thick. The epithelium varies from squamous to ciliated pseudostratified columnar (respiratory), or it may be transitional between the two. Scattered mucocytes and intraepithelial neutrophils are common. Surface keratinization is absent or scant, unless irritated by trauma or dried by air. Mitoses are rare and not atypical. Unless infected or irritated, the stroma contains few inflammatory cells. Malignant change in exophytic papilloma is extremely rare {3957337; 11236954}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Exophytic papillomas must be distinguished from cutaneous keratinizing squamous papilloma (which is much more common in the nasal vestibule), inverted sinonasal papilloma, and papillary squamous cell carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112692,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112693,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112694,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> proliferative, exophytic, and papillary growth; lined by a multilayered sinonasal-type epithelium; no high-grade squamous dysplasia; no inverted or destructive infiltrative growth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112695,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112696,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 11,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrence rates are 22&ndash;50%; recurrence is associated with inadequate excision {3957337; 7837917}. Malignant transformation is extremely rare {24519376; 26261100}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:45:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]